'''Tackey ''' (タッちゃん, ''Tatchan'') is a [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] enemy that appears in [[Legend Stages]]. It was added in [[Version 5.1 Update|Version 5.1]]. In [[The Battle Cats Unite!]], it was added in [[The Battle Cats Unite!/Patch 1.0.6 Update|Patch 1.0.6]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Tackey
|image = E 256.png
|first appearance = '''SoL''': [[Thorny Dialogue|Sub-chapter 29 - Thorny Dialogue]]
|latest appearance = '''ZL''':  [[Phantom Bluebird|Sub-chapter 11 - Phantom Bluebird]]
|money drop = 600¢ - 2,370¢
}}

==Enemy==
Tackey has low health and few knockbacks for a Dark enemy, but its Long Distance attacks can be a handful. It has a moderate attack speed and identical standing range as [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] (400), but its attacks hit an area of 600-850, resulting in a small effective range and a large blind spot.

==Strategy==
Defeating Tackey on its own isn't too much of an issue. However, this enemy exists to support melee attackers; its effective range will push back/damage your Cats greatly while they're fighting the melee enemies, hitting your backliners and midrangers. Even with low accuracy, Tackey can greatly damage your cats. However, Tackey has a large blind spot, so if a close-ranged cat (e.g. [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]], [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]], etc.) makes its way in, they can deal damage to Tackey unharmed. Tackey thus also serves as an anti-backliner.

Try using units with adequate health to tank at least one hit or fast units like such as [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Giraffe Cat]] or [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] to enter Tackey's blind spot. If all else fails or is not effective, then consider using cats with the [[Wave Attack]] ability. Examples that are usable include [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs Cat]], [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]], [[Talents|Talented]] [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] or Talented [[Dom Cat (Special Cat)|Dark Lazer]].

